  "hypothesis": "R39 produced a sparse safe signal but the proposal remained selection-head-first: the set-selection head chose a candidate and binary rescue confidence only vetoed it afterward. R40 preserves the complete R39 model and training protocol exactly and changes only runtime candidate proposal. Each ensemble head computes candidate proposal evidence as selection_probability multiplied by dedicated binary_rescue_probability. The candidate with maximum mean joint evidence is considered only if all ensemble heads independently give that same candidate the maximum joint evidence. Existing selection threshold, binary rescue threshold, four-way harm ceiling, positive margin over keep-R11, zero-harm requirement, coverage gates and promotion criteria remain unchanged.",
